1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,201
Three hundred and one blocks, forty-nine different kinds, and the whole lot fits in one

2
00:00:05,201 --> 00:00:06,896
double chest with room left over.

3
00:00:06,896 --> 00:00:12,527
Most of it is repetition — forty-six belt segments, twenty-eight encased chain drives,

4
00:00:12,527 --> 00:00:15,825
twenty-seven item vaults, twenty fluid tanks for the boiler.

5
00:00:15,825 --> 00:00:19,401
Nothing on that list is expensive, and nothing on it is clever either, which is worth

6
00:00:19,401 --> 00:00:23,511
saying now, because the part that makes this machine work is not really in the chest at

7
00:00:23,511 --> 00:00:23,708
all.

8
00:00:23,708 --> 00:00:27,864
It is the twenty filters, and the fact that no two of them are set the same way.

9
00:00:28,050 --> 00:00:32,566
Start at the boiler, because nothing here moves without it and everything else is hung

10
00:00:32,566 --> 00:00:33,588
off what it turns.

11
00:00:33,588 --> 00:00:38,743
It looks like one boiler and it is five: five separate columns of fluid tank, four

12
00:00:38,743 --> 00:00:41,762
blocks high, each with its own steam engine on top.

13
00:00:41,762 --> 00:00:47,300
Under all of them runs a row of magma blocks, and no blaze burner anywhere — magma gives

14
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:52,037
you passive heat, the lowest setting there is, and five small boilers on passive heat is

15
00:00:52,037 --> 00:00:54,927
enough for a plant this size and not a great deal more.

16
00:00:54,927 --> 00:01:00,012
Water comes up from the pool underneath through five mechanical pumps, and the pumps are

17
00:01:00,012 --> 00:01:03,693
turned by three water wheels standing in the same water they are pumping.

18
00:01:03,693 --> 00:01:06,560
Above the engines, one shaft.

19
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:12,191
That shaft is the only thing connecting this end of the room to the machine at the other

20
00:01:12,191 --> 00:01:12,679
end.

21
00:01:12,679 --> 00:01:17,160
From the boiler the line runs north along the ceiling and drops into the plant, and from

22
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:22,582
there it is chain drives most of the way — twenty-eight of them, more of this build than

23
00:01:22,582 --> 00:01:26,936
any other single component, and the part you will never see in a screenshot of it.

24
00:01:26,936 --> 00:01:28,468
Gearboxes take the corners.

25
00:01:28,468 --> 00:01:32,973
A rotation speed controller sets the pace for everything downstream, so the crusher and

26
00:01:32,973 --> 00:01:38,104
the presses and the belts all run off one number instead of being tuned against each

27
00:01:38,104 --> 00:01:38,406
other.

28
00:01:38,406 --> 00:01:42,574
And there is a stressometer on the wall, which earns its place the first time you add

29
00:01:42,574 --> 00:01:44,443
something and the whole plant slows down.

30
00:01:44,444 --> 00:01:46,348
This end is where the ore arrives.

31
00:01:46,348 --> 00:01:52,060
A mining train pulls in, parks, and empties itself through a portable storage interface

32
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:57,854
— and if it looks familiar, that is the machine from the last episode, which has no idea

33
00:01:57,854 --> 00:01:59,688
what becomes of what it drops off.

34
00:01:59,688 --> 00:02:05,273
What becomes of it is two smart chutes, one above the other, and they are the first

35
00:02:05,273 --> 00:02:08,361
showing of a pattern that runs through this entire build.

36
00:02:08,361 --> 00:02:15,234
Both are set to the same eight things: cobblestone, cobbled deepslate, gravel, flint,

37
00:02:15,234 --> 00:02:18,810
basalt, soul sand, netherrack and blackstone.

38
00:02:18,810 --> 00:02:20,551
One of them allows that list.

39
00:02:20,551 --> 00:02:22,258
The one next to it denies it.

40
00:02:22,258 --> 00:02:24,464
Same list, opposite switch.

41
00:02:24,464 --> 00:02:29,573
Everything the train dropped goes down exactly one of the two, there is no priority to

42
00:02:29,573 --> 00:02:33,485
get wrong, and nothing sits in the middle waiting for somebody to decide.

43
00:02:33,485 --> 00:02:38,129
Two crushing wheels with the controller between them, fed over a short belt loop.

44
00:02:38,129 --> 00:02:42,425
The wheels are not fussy about what you give them, which is mostly a virtue and

45
00:02:42,425 --> 00:02:47,951
occasionally a problem, because tunnel stone goes in alongside the ore and comes back out

46
00:02:47,951 --> 00:02:48,520
as gravel.

47
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:53,373
So the head of the crusher is that same trick again: one funnel set to allow crushed

48
00:02:53,373 --> 00:02:58,237
iron, gold, copper and zinc, and the funnel beside it set to deny those four and nothing

49
00:02:58,237 --> 00:02:58,597
else.

50
00:02:58,597 --> 00:03:00,757
Ore carries on into the machine.

51
00:03:00,757 --> 00:03:02,649
Everything else turns off here.

52
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:06,132
Washing comes next, and the fan looks wrong the first time you see it.

53
00:03:06,132 --> 00:03:11,809
A fan only washes what it blows over if it is blowing through water, and there is no

54
00:03:11,809 --> 00:03:14,816
water in front of this one — there is a leaf block.

55
00:03:14,816 --> 00:03:20,307
It is waterlogged, and Create reads the fluid rather than the block holding it, so as

56
00:03:20,307 --> 00:03:23,999
far as the fan is concerned it is facing a pond.

57
00:03:23,999 --> 00:03:29,038
The whole stage is a fan, a leaf and a water wheel to turn it.

58
00:03:29,038 --> 00:03:33,903
And since washing gravel gives you clay, and clay is not ore, the clay comes out here

59
00:03:33,903 --> 00:03:39,580
the way everything comes out of everywhere in this machine: allow clay on one funnel,

60
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,287
deny clay on the next.

61
00:03:41,287 --> 00:03:47,974
Six belts side by side, a funnel over each, one filter per funnel, and this is where the

62
00:03:47,974 --> 00:03:50,122
machine keeps most of its cleverness.

63
00:03:50,122 --> 00:03:52,386
Experience nuggets on the first lane.

64
00:03:52,386 --> 00:03:58,424
Lapis, emerald and diamond on the second — and each of those is listed twice there, once

65
00:03:58,424 --> 00:04:04,496
as the ore and once as the gem, because a crushing wheel handed a whole stone block gives

66
00:04:04,496 --> 00:04:06,806
you the ore back rather than what is inside it.

67
00:04:06,806 --> 00:04:08,048
Gunpowder and quartz.

68
00:04:08,048 --> 00:04:09,279
Redstone and coal.

69
00:04:09,279 --> 00:04:10,707
Copper and zinc nuggets.

70
00:04:10,707 --> 00:04:11,996
Iron and gold nuggets.

71
00:04:11,996 --> 00:04:16,071
Anything matching none of the six stays on the belt and comes round again, which means

72
00:04:16,071 --> 00:04:21,040
adding a metal later is a question of adding a lane rather than rebuilding the sorter.

73
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:25,777
Nuggets are awkward to store and worse to carry, so they get pressed on the way past.

74
00:04:25,777 --> 00:04:30,792
Three basins with a mechanical press over each, and the filter on the basin decides

75
00:04:30,792 --> 00:04:36,655
which metals are allowed to meet: redstone and coal in the first, copper and zinc in the

76
00:04:36,655 --> 00:04:39,488
second, iron and gold in the third.

77
00:04:39,488 --> 00:04:41,984
That separation is not tidiness.

78
00:04:41,984 --> 00:04:47,580
A basin with two metals in it will happily make you something — it just will not be the

79
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:48,393
thing you wanted.

80
00:04:48,393 --> 00:04:54,546
Over each output is a funnel set to the finished block, so nothing half-pressed gets

81
00:04:54,546 --> 00:04:55,359
past.

82
00:04:55,359 --> 00:05:00,688
Storage is deliberately dull: twenty-seven item vaults for bulk, and a row of twelve

83
00:05:00,688 --> 00:05:05,088
chests underneath them for the part a hopper or a hand can actually reach.

84
00:05:05,088 --> 00:05:08,699
What sits under the chests is the interesting half.

85
00:05:08,699 --> 00:05:15,781
A content observer beneath each one, a display link above, and a wall of sixteen display

86
00:05:15,781 --> 00:05:17,650
boards fed from those links.

87
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:23,734
Eight lines: the power on the network in stress units, the fill level of the storage,

88
00:05:23,734 --> 00:05:29,643
and then one line per lane — gold and iron, copper and zinc, coal and redstone,

89
00:05:29,643 --> 00:05:32,790
byproducts, valuables, experience nuggets.

90
00:05:32,790 --> 00:05:38,130
That sounds like decoration right up to the first time a lane stops quietly, and a

91
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:44,051
number that has not moved all evening tells you which of the twenty filters to go and

92
00:05:44,051 --> 00:05:44,771
look at.

93
00:05:44,771 --> 00:05:46,362
One lever starts all of it.

94
00:05:46,362 --> 00:05:52,643
Off, a redstone torch burns, the wire beside it carries fifteen, and a powered clutch is

95
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:57,983
a disengaged one — so the wheels turn nothing, the pumps stay still and the boiler stays

96
00:05:57,983 --> 00:05:58,459
dry.

97
00:05:58,459 --> 00:06:03,672
Throw it and the torch goes out and everything downstream of it wakes up at once.

98
00:06:03,672 --> 00:06:08,792
Then feed it: ore into the crusher, crushed ore onto the washer, nuggets straight onto

99
00:06:08,792 --> 00:06:13,470
the sorter, all at the same time, because a single batch takes longer to travel the whole

100
00:06:13,470 --> 00:06:19,241
line than we have here and a plant working in only its first third looks broken rather

101
00:06:19,241 --> 00:06:19,902
than busy.

102
00:06:19,902 --> 00:06:20,878
Give it a moment.

103
00:06:20,878 --> 00:06:24,941
Every lane moving, the wall counting up, and that is a Create ore plant.
